      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1930s the Civilian Conservation Corps reforested the area while the Works Progress Administration built a new county jail, Groveton High School, and a gymnasium.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/groveton-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The oldest active missionary Baptist church in Texas, organized 188 years ago, still stands in Groveton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/groveton-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Over the next three years the local mill was dismantled, and nearby rail lines were abandoned.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/groveton-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The dismantling of the mill marked the end of Groveton’s brief industrial era in the early 2000s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/groveton-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Civilian Conservation Corps’ reforestation efforts in the 1930s helped restore the pine forests that surround Groveton today.",
